From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:47:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Composite extension from X server 1.2.0

TinyX has Render, XFixes and Damage but not Composite, so no compositing
manager could run.  This brings composite/ and miext/cw/ from
xorg-server-1.2.0 and the hooks they need elsewhere, all under
#ifdef COMPOSITE (the build defines it):

- WindowRec.redirectDraw and PixmapRec.screen_x/screen_y;
- SetWinSize and SetBorderSize use the window's own box when it is
  redirected; miValidateTree takes the border clip from Composite
  (miRegisterRedirectBorderClipProc);
- Damage converts pixmap coordinates of a redirected window's backing
  pixmap to screen coordinates;
- fb offsets drawing to a window by its pixmap's screen_x/screen_y
  (without it drawing landed at screen coordinates in the small backing
  pixmap and overran the heap);
- the extension is initialised before Damage, as in 1.2.0, and is on by
  default ("-extension Composite" turns it off).

The imported code is adapted to this tree: region macros without the
screen argument, swaps/swapl without the scratch variable, malloc/free
for xalloc/xfree.  compNewPixmap sets IncludeInferiors on the scratch GC
before validating it, so that the GC cw copies to its backing GC already
has the mode.
